 ## Scope
 
+Approved quality review (A11Y-001 / MOB-001, revision 1): non-immersive public pages reserve the measured privacy panel height only while it is open. Keyboard focus is scrolled above the panel without changing consent. The compact menu has a scrollable height bounded by the measured masthead and consent panel; the immersive profile retains its separate full-screen menu and slide reservations. Editorial headers wrap the owner-provided brand and controls onto separate rows when enlarged text or a long name needs more room. No owner setting, localized copy, or public image source is replaced by these layout rules.
+
 November 2026 editorial implementation: Cadrora's profile selects `home.presentation = 'editorial'` (Direction B), a system-serif display face, semantic cream/plum surfaces, a full-width photo and editorial demo rows. It keeps the existing routes and photographer demo pages. The workflow and real-site example precede the sample sessions; installation links directly to the existing guide, and a short FAQ describes current capabilities. These product guidance sections belong to the build-time showcase profile, not to a photographer's editable content.
 
 Owner settings remain authoritative: hero text, up to six typed actions, photo revision, sessions and their order/framing, page visibility, gallery discovery, languages, theme and analytics configuration still use the existing admin and shared schemas. Every `showOnHome` session is displayed, including Home-only sessions; there is no three-card cap. The editorial Home waits for settings before mounting an image, then exposes the final owner-resolved copy and controls while the photo decodes. Photo failure cannot block the copy. The existing immersive profile's preparation and phone reveal gates are unchanged.
